# ML's `let name = init in body`: `name` is seen in `body`, and `init` sees what is around the `let`.
# A block's `let name = init;`: `name` is seen in what follows it in the block, and `init` sees the
# names before it.
scopes tools.letlang

ref Var ;
bind Bind ;
scope let Let LetStmt ;
scope block Block ;
program block ;
name Let LetStmt in own ;
outside init of Let LetStmt ;
sequential LetStmt ;
